==English==
===Etymology===
From {{term|nulli-}} + {{etyl|la}} {{term|fides||faith}} + {{term|-ian}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[sceptic]]; an [[unbeliever]] or [[atheist]].
#*'''1872''', {{w|George Eliot}}, ''Middlemarch'', 4:
#*:Celia was no longer the eternal cherub, but a thorn in her spirit, a pink-and-white '''nullifidian''', worse than any discouraging presence in the "Pilgrim's Progress."

===Adjective===
'''nullifidian'''

# Of no [[faith]] or [[religion]].
# Not trusting to faith for [[salvation]].

